    "summary": "link_source_slug demands --rationale, documents that it stores it, and then silently discards it — insert_source_slug_link is never passed the value and source_slug_links.relevance_note is the column that exists for it.",
    "failure_scenario": "`db.py link-source-slug --ref-id REF-00999 --slug threshold-and-level-access --rationale \"Frost 2020 names exterior ramp thresholds...\"` returns {\"rationale\": \"...\"} in its JSON, so the caller sees the warrant echoed back, but the row lands with relevance_note NULL. All 12 cross-file links this PR writes have relevance_note NULL (`select count(*) from source_slug_links where relevance_note is not null` → 0 of 32). D-0174 (ADOPTED) records this exact defect as measured — \"source_slug_links.relevance_note exists and is populated in 0 of 10 rows ... the adjudication is made every time and recorded never\" — and the new writer collects the adjudication and still records it never. The session doc (\"demands a --rationale naming which claim bears on the target slug\") and the attestation (\"seven of the ten cross-slug links written are my own judgement calls recorded in a free-text --rationale\") both assert a record that does not exist."
  },
  {
    "file": "scripts/migrations/data_20260918041751_2026-09-18-research-batch-15-t2-synthesis-threshold.sql",
