    "summary": "The batch retires the only live determination without a successor and without re-determining, leaving zero live specifications corpus-wide and an eighth dangling supersession pointer.",
    "failure_scenario": "After this PR `select count(*) from specifications where retired_at is null` returns 0 and spec 7's superseded_by_specification_id is NULL. retire_specification's own docstring sets the order as \"retire, re-determine, then link\"; only step 1 was performed, and the session's \"Owed\" list (GAP-010, GAP-008, GAP-009, Kim 2014, REF-00977 backward set) omits the re-determination. This reproduces the F4 defect the same author documented hours earlier in this PR's own workplan (\"retired rows are dead ends ... no keyed route to spec 7, the live determination\") and takes it further: there is now no live determination to route to. No gate catches it — determination_gates holds 0 rows and no check asserts that a parameter has a live specification."
