    "summary": "Ten commands from this session were appended to the previous session's command log before scratchpad/CURRENT was moved, splitting the batch-15 record across three folders.",
    "failure_scenario": "The added lines carry ts 2026-09-18T03:22:38Z–03:23:50Z and session_id 3ff1e851-f042-5657-9a7b-d4bf4f3aaeec — this session — but land in batch-14's record, and further commands land in batch-13's. This is the trap CLAUDE.md §7 names verbatim (\"your command log appends to someone else's record until you move it\"): batch 14's log now contains work it did not do, and batch 15's log is missing its opening orientation — including the queries that established the T2 prior the session's §1 rests on."
